Review decision: native ownership uses forced C2C_HOST_OWNED_MAILBOX=1 plus existing opt-out flags. c2c MCP, hooks and refreshed OpenCode plugin honor the marker before native side effects; host CLI remains available. Real Codex 0.163 probing disproved parent-only env inheritance (MCP launcher env_clear) and naive config/read replay (null timeout values fail TOML decoding). Explicit per-stdio environment injection and omission of normalized null settings are required. Codex host mode refuses enabled native plugins and inactive project MCP definitions it cannot safely isolate before startup; no hidden executable promotion. Native external servers and unsupported providers are not advertised as T3-owned delivery. Tests remain on x-p35; parent owns c2c guard and generated plugin alongside setup docs.

Native plugin refinement: config.plugins and plugin/list are incomplete authorities because remote installed plugin caches merge later. Host mode therefore explicitly sets features.plugins=false for its native Codex threads (documented compatibility restriction); it preserves unrelated configured MCP servers. No hand-written native plugin discovery. Inactive workspace MCP definitions still fail closed before trust transition. Native stdio ownership marker must be explicit because arbitrary inherited env is filtered.